1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,146
One receipt.

2
00:00:01,146 --> 00:00:01,942
Four items.

3
00:00:01,942 --> 00:00:03,136
Different return rules.

4
00:00:03,136 --> 00:00:07,912
ReturnWindow makes the deadlines visible, and keeps the evidence beside every decision.

5
00:00:09,017 --> 00:00:11,807
Start with a receipt and the store policy.

6
00:00:11,807 --> 00:00:15,296
You can upload a photo or PDF, or paste text.

7
00:00:15,296 --> 00:00:19,482
This walkthrough uses a synthetic receipt and a clearly labelled demo date.

8
00:00:20,583 --> 00:00:23,646
The sample is read by the actual local OCR engine.

9
00:00:23,646 --> 00:00:25,790
Nothing is sent to a receipt service.

10
00:00:25,790 --> 00:00:30,384
But local does not mean infallible: the purchase date has been read as the fifth

11
00:00:30,384 --> 00:00:30,996
of October.

12
00:00:32,117 --> 00:00:37,781
The earbuds policy allows fourteen days from purchase or delivery, so the app asks which

13
00:00:37,781 --> 00:00:38,536
date applies.

14
00:00:38,536 --> 00:00:43,823
Select delivery, enter the tenth of October, and the earbuds deadline becomes the twenty-fourth.

15
00:00:44,950 --> 00:00:47,856
Open the full receipt to check the source.

16
00:00:47,856 --> 00:00:50,399
The printed purchase date is the eighth.

17
00:00:50,399 --> 00:00:55,848
Extracted fields are editable, so a confident OCR mistake does not have to become a

18
00:00:55,848 --> 00:00:56,938
confident wrong deadline.

19
00:00:58,050 --> 00:01:00,603
Correct the purchase date to the eighth.

20
00:01:00,603 --> 00:01:04,614
The shirt moves from the fourth to the seventh of November.

21
00:01:04,614 --> 00:01:08,625
The mug moves from the twenty-sixth to the twenty-ninth of October.

22
00:01:08,625 --> 00:01:11,178
The delivery-based earbuds stay on the twenty-fourth.

23
00:01:12,283 --> 00:01:16,025
Each item links to the exact policy passage behind its result.

24
00:01:16,025 --> 00:01:20,106
The scarf is final sale, so it gets no invented return date.

25
00:01:20,106 --> 00:01:23,847
Missing or unsupported rules also produce an explicit refusal to guess.

26
00:01:24,950 --> 00:01:27,753
Download the three eligible reminders as a calendar file.

27
00:01:27,753 --> 00:01:31,802
Each event keeps its item and deadline, with a reminder for nine a.m.

28
00:01:31,802 --> 00:01:33,671
Singapore time on the preceding day.

29
00:01:34,783 --> 00:01:39,645
The evidence pack brings the results, quoted passages, answers and correction history together.

30
00:01:39,645 --> 00:01:43,011
Download the self-contained HTML, or open the print view.

31
00:01:43,011 --> 00:01:47,873
The context stays with the dates instead of disappearing behind a calendar entry.

32
00:01:48,983 --> 00:01:52,202
Reload and the case returns from local browser storage.

33
00:01:52,202 --> 00:01:54,706
The receipt image is deliberately not retained.

34
00:01:54,706 --> 00:01:56,852
Start over clears the saved case.

35
00:01:56,852 --> 00:02:01,502
There is no account, backend, or API key needed to use the app.

36
00:02:02,617 --> 00:02:08,018
The project began in an empty folder with the Devpost Learn Skill Pack.

37
00:02:08,018 --> 00:02:13,835
Scope, product requirements, specification and the build checklist stay in the repository, alongside the

38
00:02:13,835 --> 00:02:15,082
implementation and tests.

39
00:02:16,183 --> 00:02:20,527
ReturnWindow is a bounded English-policy proof of concept, not legal advice.

40
00:02:20,527 --> 00:02:24,476
Review the source and conditions before relying on a date.

41
00:02:24,476 --> 00:02:29,214
One receipt, separate clocks, and an explanation you can take with you.
